  "answers": {
    "q1_does_the_plane_over_or_understate": {
      "answer": "It overstates the *centre* of observable execution cost and sits near the tail: at the median the measured non-fee cost is 0.024697 bps against the plane's 3.353554 bps ESTIMATED non-fee allowance (136x), but the plane's allowance is *below* the p95 of realised taker cost on the worst book (4.5863 bps). It is conservative as a median estimate and roughly a p95-p99 allowance, so it is not uniformly generous and the difference is not free budget.",
      "observed": "round trip microstructure median across four books 0.024697 bps; realised aggressor round trips {'spot/BTCUSDT': 0.065705, 'spot/ETHUSDT': 0.487184}; worst book p95 4.5863 bps; worst single checkpoint 0.3680 bps",
      "assumed": "that the plane's non-fee terms were ever intended as a median rather than as a conservative allowance \u2014 the artefacts do not say which"
    },
    "q2_where_are_costs_materially_lower": {
      "answer": "Only in the fee schedule, and only by a factor of ~2.3 bps: the non-fee component measured at or near its floor (0.024697 bps median, 0.0 bps of book walk at every size up to 2000 USDT), so no re-optimisation of order placement can move a round trip by more than ~3.35 bps. The published token-discounted tier moves it by 5.0 bps, and that is an account/tier decision, not an execution-skill finding.",
      "observed": "fees are 20 of the 23.3536 bps and are KNOWN from the schedule; measured walk beyond best 0.0 bps at every size on all four books",
      "assumed": "that any future order would in fact receive the tier the schedule publishes \u2014 no account statement exists in this repository"
    },
    "q3_are_those_conditions_frequent_and_executable": {
      "answer": "The fee tier is available on essentially every taker order and therefore frequent and executable; the measured cheap execution is *evidence about a book state*, not about a fill. Nothing in the capture records order lifecycle, queue position or partial fills, so maker execution cannot be claimed as available at all.",
      "observed": "the measured window is one 4.1 h session of a single regime; 496 checkpoints; no order was placed",
      "assumed": "nothing: the maker question is reported INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE rather than assumed away"
    },
    "q4_what_explains_most_of_the_cost": {
      "answer": "The fee schedule: 85.64 % of the plane is two KNOWN exchange fee legs, which no market condition in this capture could change. Everything the venue's book contributed, at the median, is 0.11 % of the plane.",
      "observed": "plane decomposition rebuilt in-process; measured non-fee cost across four books and a 50-2000 USDT size ladder",
      "assumed": "the published fee schedule applies (a documented policy, not a measurement)"
    },
    "q5_any_asset_or_modality_worth_more_research": {
      "answer": "No asset in this seal offers a materially better net condition: the difference between the best and worst book's realised round trip (0.0657 vs 0.4872 bps) is two orders of magnitude below the fee floor, so asset selection is not where the economics are decided. The only modality that could change the answer is maker execution priced from order-level evidence, which requires a capture this campaign does not have; it is recorded as a gap, not recommended as a result.",
      "observed": "BTC and ETH only; no third asset exists in the seal",
      "assumed": "that BTC/ETH generalise to the alts in the register \u2014 they are not tested here and are not claimed to"
    },
    "q6_observed_versus_assumed": {
      "answer": "The measured layer is OBSERVED_FORWARD and cannot promote anything: the best gross edge in the register is 8.912 bps and the KNOWN fee legs alone are 20.0 bps, so even a hypothetically free non-fee component leaves 0 of the 24 cells net positive (none). The fee level, the tiers and any change to the plane are governance assumptions, not measurements.",
      "observed": "forward book, trades, latency and funding from the sealed window: 1984 checkpoints reproduced, 0 look-ahead violations, 163658 real aggressor prints joined",
      "assumed": "the fee schedule; that a static book walk approximates a live order; that one 4.1 h session represents the regimes the strategies would meet"
    }
